EastSun 20260930: "確認目前github版本，本機端測試沒問題的不要動" then "都要" (apply 77..85 and push).
cum_check2 over the union of the 9 packages (210 files): NEW 35 / OLD 162 / LOCAL 13 / GONE 0 (C++ + web; web files are in
the web commit of the same name). OLD/NEW take the laptop's last version; LOCAL are three-way merges with the package's own
base (= the laptop version merged here last time, 5f3ff7b):
  clean (11): cinitial.cpp, csystem.cpp, MachineType.h, Public/MyProductionRecord.cpp, tests/test_web_motor_access.cpp,
              WebBridgeTags.cpp, WebMotorAccess.cpp, WebMotorAccess.h + web background.html, HW.teach.html, Main.MotionView.html
  one conflict each, both sides kept:
    WebMotorAccessLive.cpp  the machine's g_W906BrakeNote line and the laptop's #include "EtherCAT/Pci1203GaliRoute.h"
                            (INDEXZ) were both written on the same blank line
    tools/wb_serve.cpp      both appended at EOF: machine HMI-KEEP + STOPBTN (W906_ExternalQuitDue), then the laptop's
                            JAM-STOP host (ForwardShowMotorErrorMessage, INBOX 118); the machine block gets back its own '}'
Checked after the merge: none of the laptop's hunks in the 13 files touch the machine's brake / power-on / M36-M40 / caption /
axis-lock / zoom / teach code (keyword scan of base->laptop), and every machine marker is still present in each merged file
(BRAKE-GROUP, G31A-TIME, BRAKE-EMPTY-AUTO3, CAPTION, SHTSPELL, MT-AXISLOCK/ALMRST, BRAKE-AXIS, STOPBTN, HMI-KEEP, BOOTSPEED).
MachineType.h: the commit takes the laptop's two new switches, both OFF (//#define WB_ENGINE_MOTOR_1203,
//#define WB_ENGINE_INDEXZ_1203). EastSun's uncommitted "// #define SOFT_SIMULTE" stays in the working tree, NOT in this commit.
README notices followed: the engine -> 1203 motor route and the Index Z1 route are the laptop's (myEthercatmotor.cpp,
EcatMotorRoute.h, Pci1203MotorRoute.cpp, Pci1203GaliRoute*, GaliRoute.h, the wb_serve install point, CMake source list) --
taken as the laptop wrote them, not edited here; both switches stay OFF. Soft limits of the 19 enabled axes are still the
+-999999 placeholders (README) -- fill before arming a route.
Applied files' mtimes set to now (Copy-Item keeps the package's). Built wb_serve in build_integ_ship_x86_o2: EXIT 0, no compile / undefined / multiple-definition line. Not run on the machine yet.

